<template>
    <heading>Startup code</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>startup</li>
        <li>module</li>
        <li>command</li>
        <li>dialog</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>This module script runs after the browser has parsed the document, so the dialog templates are available. The earlier classic script has already initialized <code><![CDATA[window.LP5.controller]]></code>.</p>
        <p>Startup dispatches a <code><![CDATA[ModalDialog]]></code> command with the logical operation key <code><![CDATA[SelectCreateProject]]></code>. The base handler uses that key to call the dialog-specific operation. The dialog's DOM template retains its separate id, <code><![CDATA[LP5-Dialog-SelectCreateProject]]></code>.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>Startup code</name>
        <code><![CDATA[
<script type="module">
    window.LP5.controller.dispatch({
        name: "ModalDialog",
        dialogName: "SelectCreateProject"
    });
</script>
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
